{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESOLUTION (rebar-debug Phase 2 complete; adopting session's final report).\n\n## How the fix landed\n\nChange 2115 (this ticket's restore: ini timeout=300, both _build-and-test.yml lanes --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread, headroom contract tests) was MERGED at a42a9d8d494 on 2026-08-22 18:16 by an operator-cast Verified+1 + Submit. The manual vote was justified by the workflow-provenance finding recorded earlier on this ticket: the Verified gate executes workflow files from TRUSTED MAIN (run 32587991195 headSha=6a5c88027c5, job 97067339850 log line ~989 still ran --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread), and pytest-timeout precedence CLI > INI meant main's stale flag overrode the patchset's ini=300 — so 2115's failing run structurally could NOT exercise its own fix, and no patchset iteration of the same config-only shape ever could.\n\n## Post-merge proof (replication of the original report — gone)\n\nGerrit Verified Gate runs at merged main a42a9d8d494 (32590300224, 32590289712): ALL pytest legs success — including ubuntu py3.13 (the coverage leg where 13-14 workers died every pre-fix run) — zero \"worker crashed\"/\"node down\". The integration (loadgroup) tier completed within its budget instead of hanging. Baseline comparison: parent 4d6c1cc835e run 32581500417 (16182 passed, 906 s, --timeout=300, zero crashes) vs pristine 6a5c88027c5 runs 32583448507/32585303586 (~11-13 worker deaths each). Main is unblocked: subsequent changes 037d4da8373 and 53eaea07aa2 landed normally through the gate.\n\n## Secondary symptom (loadgroup hang until job timeout)\n\nFixed on main by 53eaea07aa2 (ticket 8a4f-f0f4-ed92-4c70): --max-worker-restart=0 on the integration lane — under --dist loadgroup a dead worker's pending items were re-dispatched to respawned workers that died on the same item up to numprocesses*4 restarts, burning toward the 60-min job cap. The follow-up I filed for the same defect (cac1-6391-7944-470e) is now a duplicate of 8a4f; linked accordingly.\n\n## Prevention (residual risk → ticket filed)\n\nThe class defect that burned 2115 PS1 — a budget change in pyproject.toml is inert on its own gate run because trusted-main's stale --timeout CLI flag overrides ini — remains live for any FUTURE budget change. Filed 5a30-d423-b1f5-4e33 (wearable-explicable-magpie, discovered_from this ticket) carrying a fully implemented + locally validated conftest marker-floor mechanism (MARKER > CLI precedence, floor-not-blanket semantics; discriminating probe: two 25 s tests under -n 2 --dist worksteal with hostile --timeout=20 passed, zero node-downs), preserved on branch preserve/timeout-floor-hardening (commit b38bf9a4748, base a42a9d8d494; rebase over 53eaea07aa2 before use).\n\n## Defect attribution\n\ncaused_by 73b8-2d79-3046-44ce (story bold-abeyant-indri, introducing commit 6a5c88027c5 / change 2100): lowered the budget 300 s → 20 s on the strength of a local unit-tier run, below the measured 18.7-29.93 s legitimate cost band of ~14 whole-tree-scan tests on the covered legs. Close carries --class=regression --caused-by=73b8-2d79-3046-44ce."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787426854928785001,"uuid":"4fb9bb20-6a0a-4c98-9021-73274fa335ea"}